{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1ybv1BAcBgwQXRcvye5", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm not signing off. The sweep found several problems, and the developer has only confirmed one of them.\n\n**Confirmed (logged by the developer):**\n- **Split selector resets on rotation.** With Biweekly selected ($58.33), one rotation to landscape and back returns the selector to Daily ($1.9). This is the \"view-model memory\" change in this build.\n\n**Filed but answered \"could not reproduce with the steps given\":**\n- **Weekly/Biweekly use 24 days.** \"Spread over what's left of the period\" divides by 24 days (`$100 / 24 days × 7 = $29.17`). Today is 14 Nov, so 21 days are left, and Daily uses 21 (`$40 / 21 = $1.9`). The 24 is the full period length (11 Nov–4 Dec). The \"For next week\" step uses 17 days.\n- **Budget breakdown ignores today's spend.** After saving a $12.50 Food expense, Spent is $72.5 and Available is 28%. The Daily breakdown still reads \"Left of the total budget $100 − $60 = $40\" and \"$40 / 21 days = $1.9\". The later steps use $72.5 and $27.5, so the sheet disagrees with itself. The Calculated amount stays $1.9 instead of about $1.31.\n- **Weekly first step shows $0 spent.** It reads \"$100 − $0 = $100\", and Weekly stays $29.17 after the $12.50 expense, while the Spent tile shows $72.5.\n- **Leading zeros before an operator.** Typing 0, 0, 7, +, 3 shows \"$007+3\" (result \"= $10\"). Typing 0, 0, 7 alone shows \"$7\".\n- **Expense list blank in portrait.** The area above the number pad is empty in portrait, but in landscape it shows Today, Food $12.5 and Total: $12.5.\n\n**Checked and working:** the Daily/Weekly/Biweekly chips (apart from the rotation reset), the pill (\"Daily Amount exceeded / For tomorrow $1.38\"), the pill long-press breakdown, the number pad (digits, decimal, backspace, empty check, \"12.5\" entry, Food category), saving an expense (Spent and Analytics total $72.5 agree), closing the New Budget Period sheet without changes, and the draft amount surviving an app restart.\n\n**Not tested:** \"Finalize budget period early\" (it would end the period), actually applying a new budget or period, Transport category saves, \"Recurrent payment\", and the Category limits and Savings settings.\n\nWhether the four \"could not reproduce\" items are real bugs is for the developer to decide. The first two can be checked directly against the on-screen figures above."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1636, "cache_read_input_tokens": 224276, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1636}, "output_tokens": 1, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6dadd741-4414-44ff-96cc-ca1e63222dbd", "uuid": "223d6248-d0cb-46dc-8f0a-79cf97242917", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T01:46:40.511Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1ybumJ4dpgvxpQZTTGx"}
